## 🌲 Feature Branch Workflow & Isolation Guardrails

**Never commit directly to `main`.** All work must be isolated in a feature branch and verified before merging.

### Branch Naming & Creation

Before starting any feature, fix, refactor, or chore:

1. `git branch --show-current` → verify current branch.
2. If on `main`, immediately create and switch:
   - `feature/<short-description>` — new features
   - `fix/<short-description>` — bug fixes
   - `refactor/<short-description>` — code improvements
   - `chore/<short-description>` — deps/config updates
   ```bash
   git checkout -b feature/<short-description>
   # or via manager:
   node scripts/git-workflow.mjs create feature/<short-description>
   ```

### Branch Lifecycle & Verification

- Develop and test **entirely** inside the feature branch.
- Before any merge, run verification inside the branch:
  ```bash
  npx tsc --noEmit
  npx tsc -p electron/tsconfig.json --noEmit
  npx tsc -p scripts/tsconfig.json --noEmit
  pnpm exec vitest run
  # or
  node scripts/git-workflow.mjs verify
  ```
- Only proceed to merge if all checks pass.

### Safe Merging Strategy

```bash
git checkout main
git pull origin main
git merge feature/<short-description> --no-ff -m "Merge feature/<short-description> into main"
git push origin main
# also sync secondary remotes if present:
git push orgrelease main 2>/dev/null || true
git push https://github.com/YUouriii/app-BloxMind-ai.git main 2>/dev/null || true
git branch -d feature/<short-description>
# or via manager:
node scripts/git-workflow.mjs merge feature/<short-description>
```

`main` must remain clean and free of unverified code. Direct pushes to `main` without a feature branch are forbidden.

Workflow manager source of truth: `scripts/git-workflow.mjs` (also handles multi-repo remote checks via `electron/opencodeConfig.ts:resolveTargetRepo`).